# {{ title }}

A [Smeltery](https://github.com/smelteryworks/smeltery) application.

## Run it
{% if web %}
```sh
smeltery serve
```

The app listens on <http://127.0.0.1:8000> (`SERVER_HOST` and `SERVER_PORT` in `.env`). `smeltery serve` rebuilds
and restarts it when Rust code changes.{% if agents %} It also runs the agents, jobs and schedule in `app/agents/`; the
Watchfire dashboard is at <http://127.0.0.1:8000/_watchfire>.{% endif %}
{%- if alloy %}

The pages are {{ kit_name }} components in `resources/js/pages/`, rendered in the browser by Inertia; the
controllers in `app/controllers/` return them with `alloy::render("…")` and their props. Node.js and npm build
them (Node.js 20.19+ or 22.12+): run `npm install` once, then `smeltery serve` also starts the Vite dev server
(`node node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js`, on `127.0.0.1:5173`), which updates the page as files change. The
stylesheet is `resources/css/app.css`, imported by `{{ entry }}`{% if tailwind %} and built by Tailwind through
`@tailwindcss/vite`{% else %}: the forge theme, prebuilt for the kit's pages{% endif %}.

Every `VITE_` value in `.env` is compiled into the JavaScript and readable by anyone; the app writes
`VITE_APP_NAME` only.
{%- else %}

The pages are styled by `public/assets/css/app.css`, which Tailwind builds from `resources/css/app.css` and the
classes in `resources/views/`. With Tailwind installed (`smeltery tailwind:install`), `smeltery serve` rebuilds it
on every change.
{%- endif %}
{%- if alpine %}

The layout loads Alpine.js {{ alpine_version }} from `public/assets/js/alpine.min.js`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if temper %}

## Authentication

Login, registration, password reset, e-mail verification, two-factor authentication and the settings pages
(`/settings/profile`, `/settings/password`, `/settings/two-factor`) come from Temper: `app/providers/temper.rs`
turns the features on and names their pages, `app/actions/temper/` holds the forms and what they do.
`smeltery route:list` lists the routes.
{%- elif not auth %}

## Authentication

This app was created without login pages (without the `temper` building block).
`.temper(app::providers::temper::temper())` in `bootstrap/app.rs`, with the files `CLAUDE.md` lists, turns
authentication on.
{%- endif %}
{%- if hallmark %}

## API tokens

Mobile apps, desktop apps and other clients get an API token from `POST /api/tokens` (`email`, `password`,
`device_name`, and `code` for an account with two-factor authentication on), send it as
`Authorization: Bearer smt_…` to the `auth:hallmark` routes of `routes/api.rs` (`GET /api/user`), and sign it out
with `DELETE /api/tokens/current`. Hallmark stores only each token's hash; `HALLMARK_*` in `.env` change its
settings.
{%- endif %}
{%- if search %}

## Search

`smeltery make:model Post title:string body:text --searchable --all` makes a model searchable: its list page at
`/posts` searches (`?q=`), ranked and highlighted. The database keeps the full-text index current itself
(`PROSPECT_DRIVER=database`); `app/providers/search.rs` lists the searchable models.
{%- endif %}
{%- if anvil %}

## Broadcasting

`smeltery serve` also serves WebSockets at `ws://127.0.0.1:8000/app/<key>` (the key is derived from `APP_KEY`;
`ANVIL_APP_KEY` in `.env` sets it). Clients that speak the Pusher protocol (`pusher-js`, `laravel-echo`, the Pusher
libraries for mobile platforms) connect with this host and key, subscribe to the channels of
`routes/channels.rs`{% if auth %} (private ones through `POST /broadcasting/auth`){% endif %}, and receive the events
in `app/events/`.
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
```sh
smeltery work
```

`smeltery work` runs the agents, the job queue workers and the schedule registered in `app/agents/mod.rs`, until
Ctrl-C. `smeltery serve` does the same and also rebuilds and restarts the app when Rust code changes.

While it runs, these commands talk to it through `WATCHFIRE_API_ADDR` (`127.0.0.1:8001` in `.env`):

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `smeltery agents:list` | Lists the agents with their state. |
| `smeltery agents:start\|stop\|pause\|resume\|restart <name>` | Controls an agent. |
| `smeltery agents:logs <name>` | Shows an agent's recent log lines. |

`smeltery agents:runs <name>` (recent runs), `smeltery schedule:list` and `smeltery schedule:run` (run what is due
now, once) work without a running worker.
{%- endif %}

## Test it

```sh
smeltery test
```

## Build for production

```sh
smeltery build
```

The binary lands in `target/release/{{ name }}`.{% if alloy %} Before it, `smeltery build` runs `npm run build`
(after `npm ci`, or `npm install` without a `package-lock.json`, when `node_modules/` is missing), which writes the
JavaScript, the CSS and `manifest.json` into `public/build/`. Ship the `public/` folder next to the binary; the
server needs no Node.js.{% elif web %} `smeltery build` also builds a minified
`public/assets/css/app.css` with Tailwind when it is installed. Ship the `public/` folder next to the binary.{% endif %}

On a server the binary runs the setup commands itself, without the `smeltery` CLI:
{%- if web %}
`./{{ name }} key:generate`, `./{{ name }} storage:link` and `./{{ name }} migrate --force`
{%- else %}
`./{{ name }} key:generate` and `./{{ name }} migrate --force`
{%- endif %} (`--force` is required with
`APP_ENV=production`).
